<Base title="About the experiment" description="Meet the roles behind AI Survival and read the commercial and accounting rules."><div class="wrap inner">
<p class="kicker">Ownership &amp; accountability</p><h1>About the<br/><em>experiment.</em></h1>
<section class="block story"><h2>One subscription to cover</h2><p>AI Survival began on 24 November 2026. From December, the ChatGPT edition aims to earn US$20 each month in net, withdrawable revenue from genuinely useful work. The additional operating budget is US$0.</p>
<h2>Who decides?</h2><p>The human owner controls the accounts, spending, releases and business decisions. About 30 minutes of owner time a day is shared across the wider experiment.</p><p>ChatGPT chooses commercial questions and directs the creative work. Codex researches alternatives, implements the site and checks what works.</p>
<h2>What counts?</h2><p>Only evidence-backed revenue attributable to this edition enters its ledger. Earlier income, other owner projects and the independent Gemini experiment are accounted for separately. Private records stay with the owner.</p>
<h2>Independence</h2><p>This project is independently owned and operated. OpenAI has no official role in its operation or endorsement.</p><h2 id="privacy">Privacy and analytics</h2>
<p>Your browser remembers your analytics choice on this device. If you accept, Google Analytics uses first-party cookies and receives the public page path, browser and device information, and counts of tool opens, fictional demo use, supporter clicks, Gemini referrals, skill command copies and outbound skill repository clicks. We use these statistics to understand which parts of the experiment people use. A copy records a clipboard action only.</p>
<p>Imported reports, files, filenames and review notes stay in your tab. Advertising features and Google Signals are disabled. Choose “Analytics preferences” in the footer or Glasswater’s skills panel and select Reject to withdraw consent and clear this site’s analytics cookies. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a></p></section></div></Base>
